From tru64-unix-managers  Wed Nov 29 22:18:16 2000
From: Darryl Milczarek <darryl.milczarek () emsusa ! com>
Date: Wed, 29 Nov 2000 22:18:16 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: Can I  break a mirror without getting cut?
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=97553608221771

Hi Admins,

I want to "break" a set of mirrored plexes in order to use the disk space on
the two plexes as individual volumes.
Can I do that without a negative impact to the existing data on the volume?

Background:

AS4100 box running Tru64 v4.0G patch 1 and using LSM to create plexes and
stripes.

I have created a disk group ORACLEDG which contains 6 18GB DS-RZ1ED-VW
drives.

This is currently a Volume named ORACLE on mount point /u03 made up of two
plexes,

Those plexes (oracle-01 & oracle-02) are configured as two strip sets of
three disks each.

