Sorry for the delay in posting this summary -- I didn't get to implement the
solution until this past weekend.

SUMMARY:
=======

Basically, there was no definitive answer.  Opinions ranged from "it's fine
to make /tmp a symbolic link" to "absolutely do not make /tmp a symbolic
link".  It turns out that the machine we migrated from had /tmp as a link
but I decided to make it a separate mount point.

Here's what I did:

go to single-user mode
mv /tmp /o_tmp
mkfset disk04 tmp
mount disk04#tmp /tmp
{add appropriate entry to /etc/fstab}
mv /o_tmp/* /tmp

This seems to have worked fine.  We've been live with this for 3 full
(busy!) business days with no problems.  The only error message was when I
issued the 'mv /o_tmp/* /tmp' -- I got a warning about not being able to
move any of the MailBoxPidxxx files (or whatever they are).  

Thanks to everybody who helped out!


