To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: Strange TCP/IP behaviour with additional network addresses
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=97387797401838


Dear Tru64 Managers,

We are running Tru64 4.0F. Our system is configured with an
additionnal IP address (ifconfig alias ....) on its ethernet
interface. The additionnal address is part of a separate network:

ifconfig alt0 195.83.222.129 netmask 255.255.255.0
ifconfig alt0 alias 192.168.243.129

When host A (IP addr 192.168.243.1) sends an UDP paquet to
192.168.243.129, the response's from address is 195.83.222.129.

I expect to receive a reply from 192.168.243.129. This is not the
case, and break the protocol we use (XDMCP).

